  <prompt>
    Activate the 5 compose AI catalog actions on the CLIENT and prove a real compose action dispatches
    through the HTTP wire with a WebApplicationFactory /dispatch test. The dispatch plumbing
    (queue → apply-leg → orchestrator → ledger → materialize) and the admit-gate are already wired (E-20
    landed; the 422 is gone). What is still missing on the CODE side: (2.2) the toolbar buttons ship
    `bindingId:''` so they render DISABLED, and `registerComposeAiToolbarAction` is called only in tests;
    (2.3) 2 of the 5 actions (summarize-word-changes, defined-terms) have NO client trigger at all
    (absent from DEFAULT_ACTIONS; the overflow is empty); and (084) there is NO HTTP-boundary test that
    dispatches a real compose action through the real `/dispatch` route. Close Cluster 2's CODE gaps
    (2.2, 2.3) and land the 084 forcing-function test. The LIVE-ENV catalog deploy (task 047 — the 5
    Action + 5 Binding rows to spaarkedev1) and the /healthz-green flip (2.4) are OWNER-ONLY / live-env
    and are OUT OF SCOPE here — name them as the remaining prerequisite, do NOT attempt them.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Full-stack developer fluent in the compose AI toolbar (ComposeAiToolbar registration + DEFAULT_ACTIONS
    + overflow), the dispatch client seam (dispatchConsumer / the 046 composeActionBridge), the binding-id
    resolution path (how a compose action's bindingId is supplied to the toolbar), and WebApplicationFactory
    /dispatch integration tests.
  </role>

  <goal>
    All 5 compose AI actions are triggerable from the client: the toolbar buttons carry a real bindingId
    (not '') and are enabled; the 2 missing triggers (summarize-word-changes, defined-terms) are wired
    into their entry points (overflow / return-from-Word). A WebApplicationFactory test drives a real
    compose action from the HTTP body the client sends → the real `/dispatch` route → the orchestrator →
    asserts the dispatched/stored/rendered result (084 — the anti-recurrence closure that adds the real-HTTP
    /dispatch dimension none of the 3 existing test surfaces have). Cluster 2 CODE gaps (2.2, 2.3) closed;
    2.1/2.4 (deploy + /healthz) named as owner-queued.
  </goal>

