  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner-deploy-boundary">The live-env catalog deploy (047) and the /healthz flip (2.4) are OWNER-ONLY. Do NOT deploy, do NOT run pac/Dataverse writes against spaarkedev1. Name them as the remaining prerequisite for production E2E; this task closes the CODE side + the in-process 084 test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="no-invented-discriminants">Reuse the 046 dispatch seam (composeActionBridge → dispatchConsumer + existing compose_assistant_insert). Do NOT reintroduce compose_action_request / compose_edit_apply_request; do NOT add a new dispatch route or string-key routing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="no-version-suffix">Any binding/action code or config value referenced MUST NOT carry a version suffix (@v1/-v1/@vN) — it becomes cross-env cleanup cruft.</constraint>
    <constraint source="cleanGuid">If a bindingId or any Xrm-sourced GUID enters an @odata.bind or /entityset(guid) URL, wrap with cleanGuid from @spaarke/ui-components. A bindingId sent in a JSON dispatch body is not an OData URL and is not wrapped.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-030">Compose bus events use typed discriminants — zero `as any`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="no-defer">Close gaps 2.2 and 2.3 in this pass; do NOT file deferrals for the in-scope code gaps. (2.1/2.4 are owner-deploy, not a code deferral.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-hygiene">The 084 test compiles into the BFF test project — if any BFF source changes, report publish-size delta vs 49.63 MB baseline + CVE. If code-only client + test, state no BFF source change.</constraint>
  </constraints>

